+/*
+ * Jump to the newest output.
+ *
+ * Anchored to the bottom centre of the transcript, just above the composer.
+ * It is positioned against `.ai-chat` rather than against the panel so it
+ * travels with the scroller it controls, and `position: sticky` keeps it in
+ * view at the end of the scroll without taking it out of the layout - an
+ * `absolute` button would need the scroller to be its containing block, and
+ * `overflow-y: auto` already makes that true, but sticky avoids the extra
+ * `position: relative` wrapper and the stacking questions that come with it.
+ *
+ * The ring is the panel's own black rather than a shadow: on a dark theme a
+ * shadow is invisible, and the button sits over text, so it needs a hard edge
+ * to stay readable.
+ */
+/*
+ * The wrapper is what centres the button.
+ *
+ * `align-self: center` on the button itself did NOT work: `.ai-chat` is a flex
+ * column, and a sticky child with an explicit width still stretched to the full
+ * cross size - the button rendered 1190px wide, a full-width bar instead of a
+ * circle. A full-width flex wrapper with `justify-content: center` is the
+ * layout that cannot be argued with: the wrapper takes the row, the button
+ * inside it is sized by its own rules.
